contentText:
On July 10, key stakeholders in the recorded music industry came together to announce a new system for identifying fully and partially AI-generated songs.&nbsp;

Since the release of Ghostwriter’s so-called “Fake Drake” song “Heart On My Sleeve” in May 2023, the industry has been grappling with how to deal with AI-generated material on streaming services, with DSPs each proposing their own set of guidelines. That includes anything from tagging AI-generated songs as such, to enhanced streaming fraud detection, to demonetization. But Sam Duboff , global head of policy, music business at Spotify, told Billboard in 2025 that “it’s still early days for AI tech” — leaving many platforms hesitant to create any stringent long-term rules that could lead to unintended consequences.&nbsp;

